## Command

```shell
biome lint --baseline-rule=suspicious/notARule '<TEMP_DIR>/baseline_err_when_baseline_rule_is_unknown'
```

## `biome.json`

```json
{
  "linter": {
    "rules": {
      "preset": "none",
      "suspicious": { "noDebugger": "error", "noDoubleEquals": "warn" },
      "complexity": { "noUselessCatch": "error" }
    }
  }
}
```

## `a.js`

```js
debugger;
debugger;

```

# Termination Message

```block
flags/invalid ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × `suspicious/notARule` isn't a lint rule. `--baseline-rule` expects a rule as `group/rule`, e.g. `suspicious/noExplicitAny`, or a plugin as `plugin/name`.
  


```
